1
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:12,133
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:33,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:35,400
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:41,633
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,567
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,567 --> 00:00:46,533
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,467
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:54,133
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,733
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,433
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,500
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:03,367
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:06,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:09,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:12,067
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,067 --> 00:01:13,133
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,267
<i> I'm the king of Tondo.</i>

21
00:01:24,567 --> 00:01:26,967
<i>Calm down!
We're on the same side here.</i>

22
00:01:26,967 --> 00:01:29,167
<i> - Who was that?
- We can make money off this.</i>

23
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:32,833
<i> I'm not coming home until
</i>I find Samantha Jacinto's body.

24
00:01:32,833 --> 00:01:35,533
<i>I need you to help your father
save Victor.</i>

25
00:01:35,533 --> 00:01:37,967
<i>He's being transferred
to maximum security today.</i>

26
00:01:37,967 --> 00:01:39,767
<i> Bring Victor home.</i>

27
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:42,333
<i> We both know
that Sam is a strong woman.</i>

28
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:45,900
<i>I'm just an ordinary mom
worried about her daughter.</i>

29
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,567
We will not lose her, Ma, okay?

30
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:49,967
<i>I promise you that.
I will find her.</i>

31
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:54,300
<i>Betchay can't find out
that Gloria is here.</i>

32
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,200
<i>Gabo will figure out how
to get her out of here safely.</i>

33
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,800
<i>Betchay? Who's that?
Is that Gabo's mother?</i>

34
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,967
<i> Betchay is Rudy's partner.</i>

35
00:02:00,967 --> 00:02:03,233
<i>They're cutting off
the water soon.</i>

36
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:10,100
So, are you pigs happy
you got to taste good food?

37
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,733
[BETCHAY CHUCKLES, SNORTS]

38
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,167
- [OBJECT SCRAPES]
- Where are they?

39
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,600
- Who are you talking about?
- [RUDY] Betchay.

40
00:02:17,567 --> 00:02:19,867
Are you saying I'm mooching off
on you?

41
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,333
Did I say that?

42
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:24,900
Did I say you're the pig
I'm talking about?

43
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,567
I didn't say that! I was talking
about Gabo's friends!

44
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:28,833
[CHAIR RATTLES]

45
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,267
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Hey, Betchay.

46
00:02:31,033 --> 00:02:33,367
Even if I live
in extreme poverty,

47
00:02:33,367 --> 00:02:35,533
even if my saliva's
my only food,

48
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:40,467
I won't eat these food
you got from your job!

49
00:02:40,467 --> 00:02:42,967
[DANTE] That's enough.
Let's not get carried away.

50
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:44,967
- You're too much.
- That's enough.

51
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:46,167
Do you think--

52
00:02:47,733 --> 00:02:49,967
This came from an honest job.

53
00:02:49,967 --> 00:02:52,700
- I didn't kill anyone.
- I don't care!

54
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,133
That's enough, that's enough!

55
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:55,133
[DOOR SLAMS OPEN]

56
00:02:56,633 --> 00:02:58,967
I just know
you'll end up fighting.

57
00:02:58,967 --> 00:03:00,267
[DOOR SHUTS]

58
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:02,400
If you don't want to eat,
then I will!

59
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,267
[CUTLERY CLATTERS]

60
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:06,800
You think you're all that?

61
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,267
I worked so hard,

62
00:03:10,267 --> 00:03:14,500
and all I get in return
is this attitude.

63
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,800
What the hell did I do?!

64
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,067
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

65
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,900
- Gabo. Betchay's awake.
- [GABO] Pa.

66
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,667
- Did she see Gloria?
- No.

67
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:32,033
Your Auntie Mameng hid her
in the bathroom.

68
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:37,067
I work so hard so we can eat,
yet they think they're all that.

69
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:39,133
If you don't want to eat,
then don't.

70
00:03:40,767 --> 00:03:43,833
I'm the one struggling here
for their food.

71
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:48,000
- Whatever.
- Where's Rudy?

72
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:54,467
Your brother made a fuss
and went out.

73
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,000
He won't eat the food I brought.
Then don't!

74
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,467
[MAMENG]
Well, what kind of person

75
00:04:01,467 --> 00:04:04,133
can stomach eating food

76
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:07,767
without knowing
where it came from?

77
00:04:07,767 --> 00:04:10,700
You know, Betchay,
our parents taught us

78
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:14,433
to respect ourselves.

79
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:16,767
Respect yourself?

80
00:04:16,767 --> 00:04:20,133
Then eat that respect.
Pair it with rice.

81
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:21,633
You might just be full.

82
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:25,067
Pa, what are we going to do?

83
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,700
- I'll handle it.
- Alright.

84
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:38,400
You don't want to eat
my food, fine.

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,733
I'll eat it myself.

86
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:42,900
- Luckily, there's still<i> pansit.
</i>- Ma.

87
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,333
Why did you wake up?

88
00:04:45,133 --> 00:04:48,033
You're still here?
But the sun is up.

89
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:49,300
I thought you got a job?

90
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,633
I do. Uh...

91
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:53,467
I had a job yesterday.

92
00:04:53,467 --> 00:04:58,133
Gabo gave money
for Rudy's medicine

93
00:04:58,133 --> 00:04:59,933
and to fix the roof.

94
00:04:59,933 --> 00:05:01,000
As he should!

95
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:04,633
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:06,367
Uh, Auntie...

97
00:05:06,367 --> 00:05:07,433
[BETCHAY] What?

98
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,900
Uh... this is for you.

99
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:21,433
2,000 pesos?

100
00:05:22,933 --> 00:05:25,000
This isn't enough
for the stuff I need to buy.

101
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,600
Throw in a bit extra next time.

102
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,333
Okay. I'll give you more
when I get my next paycheck.

103
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:32,367
Okay.

104
00:05:44,467 --> 00:05:45,967
[WHISPERS]
Look what just happened.

105
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:47,667
She almost saw Gloria.

106
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:49,633
And she might leave
later at night.

107
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:50,833
Please, Auntie,

108
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:52,500
make sure
she doesn't see Gloria.

109
00:05:55,867 --> 00:05:58,800
Hey! What's with
all the whispering?

110
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,267
Uh, it's nothing.

111
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:03,667
We're just talking
about the roof repair.

112
00:06:04,667 --> 00:06:06,100
Uh...

113
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:08,767
you might not be able to sleep

114
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,800
when the workers
come to fix it. It'll be loud.

115
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,000
[MAMENG] Yeah.

116
00:06:13,667 --> 00:06:14,967
Maybe you want to...

117
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,333
go to the mall for a bit.
Shop for some clothes.

118
00:06:19,733 --> 00:06:22,167
Why are you rushing me
out of the house?

119
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:24,767
Oh, uh, no, it's not like that.

120
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:28,400
We just know that you're tired.

121
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,400
And you'll get annoyed
with how loud it's going to be.

122
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,433
Wow.

123
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,367
That's oddly thoughtful
of you guys.

124
00:06:35,367 --> 00:06:38,533
Is it because
I'm the manager now at BeerGin?

125
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:45,400
We know you've been taking care
of the house for so long.

126
00:06:46,033 --> 00:06:49,433
Of course, we want you
to get the rest you deserve.

127
00:06:49,433 --> 00:06:50,367
[MAMENG] Mm-hmm.

128
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,033
It's nice to hear
that you care about me too.

129
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,967
Since I can't stay here to rest,

130
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,200
I'll leave early.

131
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,267
I've got a lot of things to do
at BeerGin.

132
00:07:06,933 --> 00:07:08,367
But make sure

133
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,033
the repairs will be done today.

134
00:07:12,267 --> 00:07:18,733
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:07:18,767 --> 00:07:20,000
[MUSIC FADES]

136
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,933
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [POLICE SIREN WAILING]

137
00:07:32,467 --> 00:07:33,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

138
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:36,533
Team, remember, there'll be
no unauthorized stops.

139
00:07:36,533 --> 00:07:37,567
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

140
00:07:37,567 --> 00:07:39,000
[SEBASTIAN]
<i> Even if there's obstruction,</i>

141
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,867
we will not stop
until everything's cleared.

142
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:42,800
<i> Victor Zafra is our priority.</i>

143
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,033
No matter what happens,

144
00:07:44,033 --> 00:07:47,100
<i> we need to get him into
maximum security detention.</i>

145
00:07:48,767 --> 00:07:50,533
[CAR ENGINES REVVING]

146
00:08:01,967 --> 00:08:03,267
Keep your eyes on that vehicle!

147
00:08:03,267 --> 00:08:04,300
[GUN COCKS]

148
00:08:07,933 --> 00:08:09,967
[CAR ENGINE REVS]

149
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,633
[CAR ENGINE REVS]

150
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- Guys, guys, guys.

151
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,900
Let's hurry.
A black van is tailing us.

152
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:32,233
Someone's following us.

153
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:35,767
Arturo, it's time.

154
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:38,667
Team, there are
hostile vehicles after us.

155
00:08:38,667 --> 00:08:39,600
Stay alert.

156
00:08:41,233 --> 00:08:42,733
- Move closer to them.
- [STATIC NOISE]

157
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:47,800
[CAR ENGINES REVVING]

158
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,933
Guys, get ready to engage.

159
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,200
[GUNS COCK]

160
00:09:01,133 --> 00:09:02,167
Block them!

161
00:09:03,433 --> 00:09:05,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

162
00:09:05,767 --> 00:09:07,067
[LOUD CRASH]

163
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:13,067
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

164
00:09:13,067 --> 00:09:14,667
All units on deck!

165
00:09:14,667 --> 00:09:16,600
Team Charlie, back us up!
Cover us!

166
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:17,733
[VICTOR GRUNTS] Argh!

167
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:19,200
Team Charlie,
we're under attack!

168
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:22,800
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

169
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

170
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:27,533
Chase them down!

171
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,533
[CAR ENGINES REVVING]

172
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:30,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

173
00:09:31,233 --> 00:09:32,433
[PUDDLE SPLASHES]

174
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,333
[PUDDLE SPLASHES]

175
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,467
[GUN COCKS]

176
00:09:40,267 --> 00:09:42,033
[CAR ENGINES REVVING]

177
00:09:42,033 --> 00:09:48,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:09:54,267 --> 00:09:56,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

180
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:57,900
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [WATER SPLASHING]

181
00:09:59,467 --> 00:10:06,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

182
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,700
- Come on!
- Get ready!

183
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:16,133
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:17,167
[GROANS]

185
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,500
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

186
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,700
[GUNSHOTS]

187
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:32,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:10:32,433 --> 00:10:34,033
[SEBASTIAN] Go on, secure Zafra!

189
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:40,300
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

190
00:10:40,333 --> 00:10:41,400
[SEBASTIAN] Hurry!

191
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:49,267
[BULLETS CLANGING]

192
00:10:49,267 --> 00:10:56,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:10:57,567 --> 00:10:58,567
[VICTOR] Pa!

194
00:10:58,567 --> 00:10:59,933
[GUNSHOTS]

195
00:11:01,967 --> 00:11:04,167
[MARIANO] Get the car! Let's go!

196
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:06,100
- Don't tell me--
- Slacking off again, huh?

197
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,067
Ibyang.

198
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,167
Yes? What is it?

199
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,400
What do you know
about Mariano Zafra?

200
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,433
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:11:15,433 --> 00:11:16,500
Zafra?

202
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,100
What I know is that
he's a former cop.

203
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:22,100
Also, he's a businessman.

204
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:23,067
Why?

205
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:27,067
Papa and I met his son
last night.

206
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:28,467
Wow.

207
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,933
But he's not from my time.

208
00:11:30,933 --> 00:11:33,067
Based on what
your father told me,

209
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,433
he's a millionaire.

210
00:11:35,433 --> 00:11:36,600
Django.

211
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,833
Did you hear about the trouble
on Soriano Street?

212
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,000
What trouble?

213
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,833
They say there was a shootout.

214
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:45,700
Then everyone started running.

215
00:11:46,233 --> 00:11:48,933
Maybe the Zafras had
something to do with it.

216
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:51,600
- Galo, Udo.
- Boss?

217
00:11:51,933 --> 00:11:53,533
Head to Soriano Street.

218
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,900
Or go back to First Creek.

219
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,333
Start asking around
about what happened.

220
00:11:57,667 --> 00:11:58,700
Wait a minute.

221
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,000
Why should we get involved
in that?

222
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,100
[SNICKERS]

223
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,300
Look at you, Ibyang.

224
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,100
Don't act like
you don't know me.

225
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:08,267
This might be my chance
to get close to the Zafras.

226
00:12:09,567 --> 00:12:11,567
- Alright, move it!
- Okay, boss.

227
00:12:11,567 --> 00:12:15,567
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

228
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:19,500
When opportunities like this
come with a lot of money,

229
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,033
they shouldn't be wasted.

230
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:22,500
So what's your plan now?

231
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,267
I'll get to know Mariano Zafra.

232
00:12:25,833 --> 00:12:27,200
I'll go straight to him.

233
00:12:27,533 --> 00:12:28,900
I'll introduce myself.

234
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:33,067
And then I'll offer my services.

235
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,200
[IBYANG, MATET CHUCKLE]

236
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,267
I knew it.

237
00:12:36,933 --> 00:12:38,600
That's what I like about you.

238
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,333
You never fail
to impress me, Django.

239
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:41,600
Because I'm smart?

240
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,500
[MATET, IBYANG CACKLING]

241
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:46,733
[IBYANG] Of course not!

242
00:12:46,733 --> 00:12:49,133
I mean, you aim high.

243
00:12:49,167 --> 00:12:50,733
You're ambitious.

244
00:12:50,733 --> 00:12:52,067
That's a good thing, mind you.

245
00:12:52,067 --> 00:12:53,400
- I'm with you.
- [CHUCKLES]

246
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,767
You can ride
along with me, Ibyang.

247
00:12:55,767 --> 00:12:57,100
- Ooh!
- Bring Matet too.

248
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,700
- Sounds good?
- Wow! [CHUCKLES]

249
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,467
Lisa, are you coming?

250
00:13:00,467 --> 00:13:02,500
As long as there's money
to be made, I'm in.

251
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,567
- All you care about is money.
- Great answer!

252
00:13:04,567 --> 00:13:05,633
[LAUGHTER]

253
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,100
[SEBASTIAN] Cover me!
I'm going to follow Zafra!

254
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:09,767
[GUNSHOTS IN DISTANCE]

255
00:13:09,767 --> 00:13:10,733
Do it!

256
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:17,667
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:30,933
[GUNSHOTS]

258
00:13:30,933 --> 00:13:34,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

259
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:39,600
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:40,900
[MARIANO GROANS]

261
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,167
We're right here!

262
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:48,700
[GUNSHOTS]

263
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,800
Papa, let's go!

264
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,167
- More of them are showing up!
- [GROANS]

265
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:55,900
- [INDISTINCT SHOUTING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

266
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:58,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

267
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:00,567
Come on!
We've secured what we need!

268
00:14:00,567 --> 00:14:02,167
- Lucas!
- Let's go, let's go!

269
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:08,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:14:08,167 --> 00:14:10,133
You just had to give us
a hard time, you bastard!

271
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,167
- Hurry! Let's lock him up!
- Let's move!

272
00:14:12,167 --> 00:14:13,267
[ROBERT] Come on!

273
00:14:13,267 --> 00:14:14,533
- [VICTOR] Hmph!
- Get in!

274
00:14:16,467 --> 00:14:17,500
[SLIDING DOOR CLOSES]

275
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:23,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

276
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:31,867
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:38,200
[POLICE OFFICER]
Alright, throw him in.

278
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,300
This is where you'll rot.

279
00:14:48,433 --> 00:14:52,500
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

280
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:56,667
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:59,933
[GATES RATTLING, CREAKING]

282
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:06,400
[INMATES SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY]

283
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,533
[GATE HANDLE CLANKS, SQUEALS]

284
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:09,933
[GATE CREAKING]

285
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:13,467
[GATE HANDLE CLANKS, SQUEALS]

286
00:15:15,967 --> 00:15:17,067
[KEYS JINGLE]

287
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,433
[LOUD BANGING]

288
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:27,900
Love.

289
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,667
Why don't you want her
to see me?

290
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:31,533
When she woke up,

291
00:15:31,533 --> 00:15:34,200
everyone scrambled to hide me.

292
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:36,433
L-Love, I'm so sorry.

293
00:15:36,467 --> 00:15:39,433
Auntie Betchay just
doesn't know you yet.

294
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:42,300
If she finds out you're here
in my room,

295
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,400
she might get mad.

296
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,600
[STAMMERS]

297
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,333
And I don't want you two
to get off on the wrong foot.

298
00:15:46,333 --> 00:15:47,467
So...

299
00:15:47,467 --> 00:15:49,667
I'm sorry we have
to keep hiding you.

300
00:15:49,667 --> 00:15:50,767
But don't worry.

301
00:15:50,767 --> 00:15:52,533
We'll introduce you
to each other in time.

302
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,167
[SIGHS]

303
00:15:54,167 --> 00:15:55,300
I don't get it.

304
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:58,167
Why does it seem like
she hates you?

305
00:16:00,433 --> 00:16:01,467
[INHALES DEEPLY]

306
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,533
Honestly...

307
00:16:06,067 --> 00:16:07,333
I don't know either.

308
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:09,667
She has hated me...

309
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:10,767
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:16:10,767 --> 00:16:12,700
since I was a kid.

311
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:15,967
She's always held a grudge
against me.

312
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,667
When I was a young boy...

313
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,433
<i> Do you still have mangoes?</i>

314
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:23,700
- [VENDOR]<i> We've run out.
</i>- [WOMAN WHIMPERS]

315
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,133
<i> Want me to help you?</i>

316
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:27,500
<i>- Sure. Help me carry this.
- Alright, I'll just buy this.</i>

317
00:16:27,867 --> 00:16:28,867
<i> This way.</i>

318
00:16:29,433 --> 00:16:31,233
<i>- You can drop it right here.
- Okay.</i>

319
00:16:31,233 --> 00:16:32,367
<i>- There we go.
- Thank you.</i>

320
00:16:32,367 --> 00:16:33,667
<i> What's your name?</i>

321
00:16:33,667 --> 00:16:34,667
<i> Gabriel.</i>

322
00:16:34,667 --> 00:16:35,867
[WOMAN] What a beautiful name.

323
00:16:35,867 --> 00:16:37,333
<i> May the Lord bless you.</i>

324
00:16:37,333 --> 00:16:39,500
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

325
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:40,633
[YOUNG BETCHAY] Gabriel!

326
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:43,600
<i>Mama Betchay, I was just
helping a pregnant woman!</i>

327
00:16:43,633 --> 00:16:45,067
<i>- You're so stubborn!
- [JEEPNEY HORN HONKING]</i>

328
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:46,400
<i> Come back here!</i>

329
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

330
00:16:47,367 --> 00:16:48,500
[MAN] Hey!

331
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,600
[DRIVER] Are you trying
to get yourselves killed?!

332
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,267
<i> Want me to slash your tires?!</i>

333
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:53,367
<i>- You--
- Shut up!</i>

334
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,533
<i>- Watch your own son!
- All you do is talk!</i>

335
00:16:55,533 --> 00:16:56,667
<i> Come here, son!</i>

336
00:16:56,667 --> 00:16:58,600
<i>- Didn't you see the kid?!
- What a bastard!</i>

337
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,733
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

338
00:16:59,733 --> 00:17:00,933
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [LOUD CRASH]

339
00:17:00,933 --> 00:17:03,300
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

340
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,533
<i> Mama Betchay!</i>

341
00:17:04,933 --> 00:17:06,467
<i> Mama Betchay!</i>

342
00:17:06,467 --> 00:17:08,367
<i> Mama! Help us!</i>

343
00:17:08,367 --> 00:17:09,533
<i> Mama Betchay!</i>

344
00:17:09,533 --> 00:17:11,900
<i> - We need help!
</i>- [WAILING]

345
00:17:12,667 --> 00:17:14,267
<i> Mama Betchay...</i>

346
00:17:14,267 --> 00:17:16,167
<i> Are you feeling okay?</i>

347
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,300
<i> Get out of my room.</i>

348
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:23,433
<i> Mama Betchay, I'm sorry.</i>

349
00:17:23,433 --> 00:17:25,400
<i> Don't be angry anymore.</i>

350
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:27,900
<i> You're my mother, right?</i>

351
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:33,967
[INDISTINCT CHATTER IN DISTANCE]

352
00:17:33,967 --> 00:17:36,100
[BREATH QUIVERING]

353
00:17:38,333 --> 00:17:39,600
<i> I'm not angry.</i>

354
00:17:43,367 --> 00:17:45,533
<i> I'm furious!</i>

355
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,267
[SOBS] Mama Betchay!

356
00:17:47,267 --> 00:17:49,067
<i> Please stop being angry!</i>

357
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:50,833
<i> You're not my son!</i>

358
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,633
[YOUNG MAMENG] Betchay?

359
00:17:53,067 --> 00:17:54,267
- [SOBBING]
<i> - Betchay!</i>

360
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:55,500
<i> That's enough.</i>

361
00:17:56,133 --> 00:17:57,733
<i> No one wanted this to happen.</i>

362
00:17:57,733 --> 00:18:00,633
<i> Don't take it out on Gabriel.</i>

363
00:18:00,633 --> 00:18:02,200
[VOICE QUIVERING] Mameng...

364
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,400
[BOTH SOBBING]

365
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:07,733
<i> I can't have children anymore
because of Gabriel.</i>

366
00:18:07,733 --> 00:18:10,633
<i> I'll never be a real mother.</i>

367
00:18:10,633 --> 00:18:14,167
<i>I'm not going to have a family
of my own.</i>

368
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:17,900
And you want me to forgive him?

369
00:18:18,467 --> 00:18:19,933
<i> Go away!</i>

370
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,900
<i> I said, go away!</i>

371
00:18:21,933 --> 00:18:23,500
<i>- Let's go, Gabriel.
- Just go!</i>

372
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,633
<i> Is it my fault</i>

373
00:18:25,633 --> 00:18:28,267
<i>that she lost her child
because of me?</i>

374
00:18:28,267 --> 00:18:30,000
<i>- No, no...
- [SOBBING]</i>

375
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,533
<i> No one is to blame.</i>

376
00:18:31,533 --> 00:18:33,500
<i>- It was an accident.
- [SNIFFLING]</i>

377
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:36,833
Your Mama Betchay lost the baby

378
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:38,900
<i>because she didn't know
she was pregnant.</i>

379
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:45,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:18:46,433 --> 00:18:49,400
[PLATES CLATTERING]

381
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,500
<i>- Those aren't for you.
- [GLASS THUDS]</i>

382
00:18:52,967 --> 00:18:54,767
- [PLATE RATTLES]
- [UTENSILS CLINK]

383
00:18:56,967 --> 00:18:59,433
<i> I'm hungry.</i>

384
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:00,833
<i> Then find your own food.</i>

385
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:02,900
<i> I don't have any money.</i>

386
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,600
<i> So, what now?</i>

387
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,733
<i>What, are you going
to keep relying on me?</i>

388
00:19:06,733 --> 00:19:09,833
<i> From now on,
you'll fend for yourself.</i>

389
00:19:09,833 --> 00:19:11,900
<i> Out there in the trash heap.</i>

390
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,433
<i>You get it?
Start collecting scraps.</i>

391
00:19:13,433 --> 00:19:16,233
<i> And when you return,
make sure you've got money.</i>

392
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:18,667
<i> Make yourself useful.</i>

393
00:19:18,667 --> 00:19:20,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

394
00:19:20,933 --> 00:19:22,533
<i> This one's mine, okay?</i>

395
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,967
<i> Mmm.</i>

396
00:19:29,633 --> 00:19:31,667
<i> - Whoa, I hit the jackpot!
</i>- [FLY BUZZING]

397
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:33,367
<i> A fly!</i>

398
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,400
[SCRAPS RATTLING]

399
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,867
<i>- Here you go.
- Let me see.</i>

400
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:43,267
<i> That comes to forty pesos.</i>

401
00:19:47,867 --> 00:19:48,900
[GIGGLES]

402
00:19:49,233 --> 00:19:51,100
<i> This looks good!</i>

403
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:55,400
- [TRAFFIC NOISE]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

404
00:19:55,400 --> 00:20:02,167
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,367
<i> Dear?</i>

406
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:06,700
<i> Can I have some of your food?</i>

407
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:13,667
[INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER]

408
00:20:15,567 --> 00:20:18,567
You can have all this, Grandma.

409
00:20:19,367 --> 00:20:20,367
[HORN HONKING IN DISTANCE]

410
00:20:20,367 --> 00:20:22,667
<i> Thank you so much, dear.</i>

411
00:20:22,667 --> 00:20:28,600
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

412
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:30,367
<i> You can have this too.</i>

413
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:32,300
<i> So you can buy medicine.</i>

414
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,700
<i> Thank you very much, dear.</i>

415
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,800
<i> May the Lord always bless you</i>

416
00:20:36,833 --> 00:20:38,967
<i> for your good heart.</i>

417
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:47,833
[DOOR CLICKS]

418
00:20:53,633 --> 00:20:54,867
<i> Here you go, Mama.</i>

419
00:20:57,133 --> 00:20:58,167
<i> That's it?</i>

420
00:20:58,167 --> 00:20:59,233
<i> Two pesos?</i>

421
00:20:59,233 --> 00:21:02,000
I gave my money to an old lady.

422
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,600
<i>She needed it more
because she was sick.</i>

423
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:08,000
<i> What old lady?</i>

424
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,867
<i> Are you lying to me?</i>

425
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:12,433
<i>This is all that's left
of my money.</i>

426
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:14,700
[COINS CLINK]

427
00:21:15,933 --> 00:21:17,533
<i> Why?</i>

428
00:21:17,533 --> 00:21:18,733
<i> Hmm?</i>

429
00:21:18,733 --> 00:21:20,967
<i> Are you rich enough to be
giving away money?</i>

430
00:21:20,967 --> 00:21:22,733
<i>You have the heart
to help other people,</i>

431
00:21:22,733 --> 00:21:25,400
<i>- but all I get is two pesos?
- [COINS CLATTER]</i>

432
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,900
<i> You're not thinking.</i>

433
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:29,500
<i>I financed your father's
auto repair shop.</i>

434
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:32,300
<i>I gave him everything
and left nothing for myself.</i>

435
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:33,600
<i> - Come here.
</i>- [YOUNG GABO WHIMPERS]

436
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,533
<i> It's time for you to grow up!</i>

437
00:21:37,267 --> 00:21:39,300
<i> Do not come home empty-handed.</i>

438
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,400
<i> Do you understand?</i>

439
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,900
<i> Yes, Mama.</i>

440
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:44,367
<i> Go on! Get!</i>

441
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:51,367
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

442
00:21:59,233 --> 00:22:00,733
<i> Hey! Hey! Hey!</i>

443
00:22:00,733 --> 00:22:02,033
<i> That's my spot!</i>

444
00:22:02,033 --> 00:22:03,467
<i> That's my food!</i>

445
00:22:04,767 --> 00:22:06,900
<i> Get out of here!
Get lost!</i>

446
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:08,533
<i> This is my spot!</i>

447
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:09,867
<i> This freaking kid.</i>

448
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:20,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

449
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:23,933
- [CAT MEOWS]
<i> - There's more here!</i>

450
00:22:23,933 --> 00:22:25,267
<i> Come on! Hurry!</i>

451
00:22:25,267 --> 00:22:27,000
<i>- Come on!
- Alright.</i>

452
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,967
<i>- Faster.
- Here.</i>

453
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,833
<i>- This is good.
- Here's some more.</i>

454
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:34,833
<i>- Jackpot!
- Hey!</i>

455
00:22:34,833 --> 00:22:35,933
<i> What are you doing?</i>

456
00:22:35,933 --> 00:22:37,267
<i>- This is our territory!
- Let's get out of here!</i>

457
00:22:37,267 --> 00:22:38,367
<i> Run!</i>

458
00:22:40,867 --> 00:22:43,000
<i> Hey! Didn't you hear us?</i>

459
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,933
<i> I'm looking for scraps!</i>

460
00:22:44,933 --> 00:22:46,767
<i> We're all starving here!</i>

461
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:51,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

462
00:22:51,933 --> 00:22:53,233
<i> What did you say?</i>

463
00:22:55,733 --> 00:22:58,367
<i> Why are you here on our turf?!</i>

464
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:00,300
<i> Hey.</i>

465
00:23:01,533 --> 00:23:03,233
[YOUNG GABO GRUNTS]

466
00:23:03,233 --> 00:23:04,300
- [GRUNTS]
- [BOY GROANS]

467
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:06,333
<i> You think you're tough?</i>

468
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:07,300
- [YOUNG GABO GRUNTS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

469
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:08,600
<i> Come on!</i>

470
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:10,233
<i> Hold on.</i>

471
00:23:10,233 --> 00:23:13,033
<i>Join our group.
We have food.</i>

472
00:23:13,033 --> 00:23:14,300
<i> You won't go hungry.</i>

473
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:21,233
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

474
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:22,933
<i> I'm Django.</i>

475
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:24,133
<i> Gabriel.</i>

476
00:23:25,567 --> 00:23:26,667
<i> Come on.</i>

477
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,700
[VEHICLE HONKING]

478
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:37,500
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

479
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:39,067
[VEHICLES HONKING]

480
00:23:43,467 --> 00:23:50,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

481
00:23:50,467 --> 00:23:53,800
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

482
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:58,700
[PHONE RINGING]

483
00:23:59,533 --> 00:24:01,133
<i> - Hello?
</i>- [MAN] Django.

484
00:24:01,133 --> 00:24:02,733
<i> Gabo spotted a truck.</i>

485
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:03,700
<i> Alright.</i>

486
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:05,600
<i> We're ready.</i>

487
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:07,900
<i>Target's on the move!
Get into position!</i>

488
00:24:07,900 --> 00:24:09,467
<i>- Move!
- Come on!</i>

489
00:24:11,333 --> 00:24:12,533
[SMACKS] Let's go!

490
00:24:12,533 --> 00:24:13,667
[ENGINES REV]

491
00:24:13,667 --> 00:24:20,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

492
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:24,367
[THUD]

493
00:24:24,367 --> 00:24:31,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

494
00:24:31,767 --> 00:24:32,967
[LATCH CRANKS]

495
00:24:39,433 --> 00:24:41,600
[BOXES CLATTER]

496
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:46,967
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

497
00:24:46,967 --> 00:24:49,033
[DJANGO]<i> Give them
</i> two more boxes.

498
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,633
<i> Hand over the money.</i>

499
00:24:52,667 --> 00:24:54,167
<i>- Django.
- How much is this?</i>

500
00:24:54,167 --> 00:24:55,267
<i> 4,000 pesos.</i>

501
00:24:56,167 --> 00:24:57,600
<i> 4,000 pesos?</i>

502
00:24:57,600 --> 00:24:59,667
<i> Are you trying to trick me?!</i>

503
00:24:59,667 --> 00:25:02,500
<i> Of course not.
I was just kidding.</i>

504
00:25:02,533 --> 00:25:04,433
<i>Cut it out.
We have orders to deliver.</i>

505
00:25:04,433 --> 00:25:05,800
<i> There.</i>

506
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:08,867
<i> That's more like it!
Move!</i>

507
00:25:08,867 --> 00:25:11,333
<i>- Hey! You two.
- Alright, next.</i>

508
00:25:11,333 --> 00:25:13,967
<i> - How much, Django?
- 3,500 pesos.</i>

509
00:25:13,967 --> 00:25:15,433
<i> - That's too expensive.
- No, it's not.</i>

510
00:25:15,433 --> 00:25:17,533
<i> You'll make a huge profit
with that!</i>

511
00:25:17,533 --> 00:25:20,000
<i> We put our lives on the line
to get those.</i>

512
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:20,933
<i> Get!</i>

513
00:25:21,633 --> 00:25:25,033
<i> Alright. That's more like it.</i>

514
00:25:25,033 --> 00:25:28,433
<i> Gabo, this is for you.</i>

515
00:25:28,433 --> 00:25:31,167
<i> - What's this?
- I told you, Gabo.</i>

516
00:25:31,167 --> 00:25:32,867
<i> We're going to be rich.</i>

517
00:25:32,867 --> 00:25:35,967
<i>I'm the brain,
you're the brawn.</i>

518
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,367
[DJANGO LAUGHS]

519
00:25:37,367 --> 00:25:39,267
<i>- Here.
- Alright!</i>

520
00:25:39,267 --> 00:25:41,233
<i> Everyone's happy!</i>

521
00:25:41,233 --> 00:25:43,767
<i>- Yes!
- Gabo never misses!</i>

522
00:25:43,767 --> 00:25:45,233
<i>- Jackpot!
- Yes.</i>

523
00:25:45,233 --> 00:25:46,833
<i> Wait a minute.</i>

524
00:25:46,833 --> 00:25:50,267
<i>Django, buddy,
why is my cut so small?</i>

525
00:25:50,267 --> 00:25:52,367
<i> Oh, come on, man.</i>

526
00:25:52,367 --> 00:25:54,733
<i> I'll treat you to booze
and ladies tonight!</i>

527
00:25:54,733 --> 00:25:56,567
<i>- Awesome.
- [LAUGHTER]</i>

528
00:25:56,567 --> 00:25:58,333
<i> Thanks, Django!</i>

529
00:25:58,333 --> 00:26:00,600
<i> Alright. Back to work.</i>

530
00:26:04,333 --> 00:26:06,033
<i> Pa?</i>

531
00:26:06,033 --> 00:26:07,367
<i> Pa!</i>

532
00:26:07,367 --> 00:26:08,467
<i> Ma.</i>

533
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,133
<i> I brought home some food.</i>

534
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:15,800
Pa, I brought home some pagpag.

535
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:17,267
<i> Where did you get that?</i>

536
00:26:17,267 --> 00:26:18,433
<i> Where'd you get the money?</i>

537
00:26:18,433 --> 00:26:21,433
<i>- A side job.
- What side job?</i>

538
00:26:23,367 --> 00:26:30,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

539
00:26:30,333 --> 00:26:35,300
<i> Pa... I have some money left.</i>

540
00:26:36,667 --> 00:26:40,333
<i> I want you to have it, Ma.</i>

541
00:26:41,233 --> 00:26:44,033
You think this will win me over?

542
00:26:44,067 --> 00:26:45,200
<i> Betchay.</i>

543
00:26:46,967 --> 00:26:48,767
<i> And don't call me Mama.</i>

544
00:26:48,767 --> 00:26:50,567
<i> You're not my son.</i>

545
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:54,667
<i>I will never forget
what you did to me.</i>

546
00:26:54,667 --> 00:26:57,433
<i>You are the reason
I lost my baby,</i>

547
00:26:57,433 --> 00:26:59,467
<i>and you can never
bring my baby back.</i>

548
00:26:59,467 --> 00:27:00,933
<i> Betchay, enough.</i>

549
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:03,733
<i>Enough?
Fine, side with your son again.</i>

550
00:27:04,567 --> 00:27:06,633
<i> What I said is true!</i>

551
00:27:07,933 --> 00:27:11,933
<i> I will never forgive him.</i>

552
00:27:13,233 --> 00:27:17,433
<i> He killed his own sibling.</i>

553
00:27:18,433 --> 00:27:25,333
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

554
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,433
<i> Why is Mama Betchay like that?</i>

555
00:27:33,933 --> 00:27:35,933
<i> No matter what I do...</i>

556
00:27:38,033 --> 00:27:40,333
<i> it's never enough for her.</i>

557
00:27:40,333 --> 00:27:43,267
I didn't want my sibling to die.

558
00:27:43,267 --> 00:27:45,200
<i> I didn't want that to happen.</i>

559
00:27:47,333 --> 00:27:49,400
<i> But why do I get the blame?</i>

560
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:55,400
Since then,

561
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,367
she has hated me.

562
00:27:59,733 --> 00:28:01,867
I didn't mean for that
to happen.

563
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:04,967
I didn't mean for
my sibling to die.

564
00:28:09,533 --> 00:28:10,900
That makes two of us.

565
00:28:12,433 --> 00:28:14,500
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

566
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:15,767
What do you mean?

567
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:22,933
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

568
00:28:26,067 --> 00:28:29,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

569
00:28:29,167 --> 00:28:30,333
Uh... [CHUCKLES]

570
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:34,300
What I meant to say is,
poor you.

571
00:28:35,933 --> 00:28:37,400
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

572
00:28:38,367 --> 00:28:39,500
It's alright.

573
00:28:40,333 --> 00:28:42,400
I'm used to Aunt Betchay.

574
00:28:43,333 --> 00:28:45,267
I choose to be
patient with her.

575
00:28:47,133 --> 00:28:48,333
What about you?

576
00:28:49,033 --> 00:28:51,567
Are you doing okay
here at home?

577
00:28:51,567 --> 00:28:55,767
Sorry about our room.

578
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,900
It's small, but...

579
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:59,600
it'll do, right?

580
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:02,067
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

581
00:29:02,067 --> 00:29:04,033
Who is he talking to?

582
00:29:05,867 --> 00:29:07,000
It's Aunt Betchay!

583
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:07,967
Be quiet.

584
00:29:07,967 --> 00:29:10,867
[CURIOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

585
00:29:10,867 --> 00:29:13,900
- Hide, Gloria! Hide!
- [SAM GRUNTS, GROANS]

586
00:29:13,900 --> 00:29:14,833
Come on!

587
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:17,667
Hide!

588
00:29:17,667 --> 00:29:18,900
Be quiet!

589
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:20,000
She might hear us.

590
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,867
- Why are we hiding?
- Shh!

591
00:29:21,867 --> 00:29:28,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

592
00:29:31,533 --> 00:29:33,533
<i> I couldn't do this
with my wife!</i>

593
00:29:33,533 --> 00:29:34,600
<i> She's not this light!</i>

594
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:36,333
<i>- Kulas!
- Oh, no!</i>

595
00:29:36,333 --> 00:29:38,900
<i>- Diday! No!
- I will chop you up!</i>

596
00:29:38,900 --> 00:29:41,233
<i> Our ratings are doing good!</i>

597
00:29:41,233 --> 00:29:43,933
<i>As long as you keep attacking
General Jacinto and the NLEA!</i>

598
00:29:43,933 --> 00:29:45,600
<i> I'm not afraid of them.</i>

599
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:47,500
<i> Where is my daughter?</i>

600
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:48,900
<i>If you really are
doing everything,</i>

601
00:29:48,900 --> 00:29:50,600
<i> you would've found Sam by now!</i>

602
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:53,800
<i>Victor Zafra has been moved to
the maximum security facility.</i>

603
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:56,133
<i> Don't forget,
my daughter is still missing.</i>

604
00:29:56,133 --> 00:29:58,600
<i> Don't stop until you find her.</i>

605
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:01,400
<i> I had Victor.
We were about to escape.</i>

606
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:02,800
<i> We still have Pia.</i>

607
00:30:02,833 --> 00:30:06,133
<i> I don't know how the Zafras
know our every move.</i>

608
00:30:06,133 --> 00:30:07,533
<i> It's either we're bugged,</i>

609
00:30:07,533 --> 00:30:11,767
<i>or they have an insider
within the NCIA.</i>

610
00:30:11,767 --> 00:30:13,767
<i>We've taken down
Samantha Jacinto.</i>

611
00:30:13,767 --> 00:30:16,467
<i>That guy she encountered
at Chinatown is next.</i>

612
00:30:16,467 --> 00:30:18,667
<i> Love, I brought homepagpag.</i>

613
00:30:18,667 --> 00:30:22,033
<i>- What's pagpag?
- It's leftover food</i>

614
00:30:22,033 --> 00:30:24,067
<i>we get from
various restaurants.</i>

615
00:30:24,067 --> 00:30:25,667
<i> I don't think she likes it.</i>

616
00:30:25,667 --> 00:30:27,567
<i>It'll taste better
if I feed it to her.</i>

617
00:30:27,567 --> 00:30:29,700
<i>He's pretending
they're husband and wife.</i>

618
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:31,967
<i> But what if she
regains her memories?</i>

619
00:30:31,967 --> 00:30:34,967
<i>What if Gabo
falls in love with her?</i>

620
00:30:34,967 --> 00:30:37,300
<i> Is this Gabo's motorcycle?</i>

621
00:30:37,333 --> 00:30:40,033
<i>Does he do illegal stuff
with this?</i>

622
00:30:40,033 --> 00:30:41,433
<i> I don't think so.</i>

623
00:30:41,433 --> 00:30:43,233
<i>Since Gabo got out of prison,
he has changed for the better.</i>

624
00:30:43,233 --> 00:30:46,000
<i>He only went to jail in the
first place because of Django.</i>

625
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,100
<i> What do you want us to do?</i>

626
00:30:47,100 --> 00:30:49,600
<i> I saw the men
who are looking for her.</i>

627
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:52,233
<i>We can't let Gloria
out of the house.</i>

628
00:30:52,233 --> 00:30:55,533
<i> Wow.
You really care about me.</i>

629
00:30:55,533 --> 00:30:57,400
<i> I thought it was all for show.</i>
